,"target_id":"b393-6784-35de-4ed4"},{"link_uuid":"241a713a-da1a-409f-8135-1946d648d4d6","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ce95-3fe5-ac9a-4f95"},{"link_uuid":"6dc71474-0128-4cbf-a7e5-cefcad016fa8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8184-df68-197a-4855"},{"link_uuid":"535ac2ae-2954-468c-8534-e727d117eb30","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8b19-8a34-c2b4-4140"},{"link_uuid":"06ae2a9e-6f16-4b48-aace-31d243f394f8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ee55-18d2-47bb-409b"},{"link_uuid":"58d27e41-8a62-4c5c-8555-ed5c8e7da6f2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c363-e76c-c731-41d8"},{"link_uuid":"4831b958-bdc9-47e4-8608-151b69654d6d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"45ff-4c69-f86b-4a72"},{"link_uuid":"0cc47a82-b4d2-42a8-ba76-88d614e6978b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6fc2-0912-dac7-4b77"},{"link_uuid":"c58a9165-7d18-43b4-a681-359b69857c49","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0e22-8fa2-a8e9-4d7e"},{"link_uuid":"850aae6c-0260-4520-88ec-8b574bac2eb8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"cc32-920f-987d-4368"},{"link_uuid":"85d05b98-f0b5-423c-b2bb-45b024b74cb5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1c67-52e8-b726-4034"},{"link_uuid":"9f5b2cc2-b7aa-4d0e-8a6b-2b3c8341498c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"867e-18c6-1428-451f"},{"link_uuid":"59902dbb-f154-45c0-8f35-af71d5d7545b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a562-53e9-fbe8-4c1f"},{"link_uuid":"015cf74a-26c2-465c-ae59-ad723beb8efc","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"e40e-c62d-a620-45ce"},{"link_uuid":"18099cbb-ebef-4fa5-ac37-4b618d8c32be","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"9581-fd6d-9a68-4bab"},{"link_uuid":"a7bc5e88-1bac-41da-89fc-8a7a4608ea99","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f355-8dfe-9021-4f6a"},{"link_uuid":"d9bae403-75e3-4b03-92df-8fa05830d4be","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"02f2-e069-bed2-40a5"},{"link_uuid":"0ca7a40e-744e-445c-8b0e-bfe016eb04b1","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"fd17-d906-a0c4-4bf2"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py:multiple measured/history blocks; strongest 348-384, 430-464, 554-565, 755-785` — Preserve parity calculations and polarity. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py:1-23, 136-141, 203-209, 261-266, 342-356` — Preserve colon-bearing model identifier parsing. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_provider_session_guard.py:1-17` — Preserve provider-session lifetime behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_push_expected_contention_quiet.py:1-27` — Preserve suppression of expected self-healing outcomes. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_push_narrow_refspec.py:1-24` — Preserve convergence under narrow refspecs. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_push_pending_marker.py:1-20` — Preserve durable push-failure signaling. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py:1-16` — Preserve untracked-overwrite recovery. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_push_rejection_surfacing.py:1-29` — Preserve remote-policy failure propagation. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_push_retry_stash_pop.py:1-14` — Preserve stash-pop conflict handling. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_push_strict.py:300-303, 395-401, 483-488` — Preserve strict push failure behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py:543-553, 606-609` — Preserve runner seam behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py:1-15, 374-384, 683-691` — Preserve AST lint scope and exclusions. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py:1-21` — Preserve facade freshness parity. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_reads_cli_search_ready_gate.py:1-17` — Preserve unusable-store rejection. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_reads_cli_uninitialized_store.py:1-18` — Preserve absent-versus-empty CLI behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py:1-32, 145-156, 187-201 and later historical docstrings` — Preserve absent-versus-empty library behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step0.py:1-13` — Preserve orient-before-debug ordering. Consumer: none found.\n- `tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py:1-17` — Preserve sibling-class review requirements. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py tests/unit/test_provider_session_guard.py tests/unit/test_push_expected_contention_quiet.py tests/unit/test_push_narrow_refspec.py tests/unit/test_push_pending_marker.py tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py tests/unit/test_push_rejection_surfacing.py tests/unit/test_push_retry_stash_pop.py tests/unit/test_push_strict.py tests/